    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0280" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">874.00/7–2545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative in Bulgaria</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Barnes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-25T18:00:00+02:00">July 25, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 26—9:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>382. Senior Regent Ganev told me last night that the decision of the Govt to go
                    ahead with elections as reported in my telegram 381 of today’s date,<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d257-f1"/> may go sour on the Prime Minister and the
                    Communists. He said that Petkov is seriously considering an appeal in [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">to</hi>] <pb facs="0281" n="269" xml:id="pg269"/> the
                    three principal Allies by a letter to be sent to the three members of Allied
                    Control Commission in which he will raise the question of whether the Yalta
                    declaration on liberated Europe is to be applied in Bulgaria.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Moscow as 197.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Barnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
